  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe wire contour of a drawn line-and-arc profile (#3937) moves each arc onto its lattice centre with its radius kept. Two neighbour arcs with different centres then end a small distance apart. Before this change, `stitch` in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/arc_cut.rs` wrote a connector line across that gap. The post rounded that line to the arc end, so each tangent joint gave a `G1` block with no motion.\n\nThe cause is in `stitch`: an arc followed by an arc with a different end always got a `Span::Line` joiner. In the test oval below, each joiner is about 5e-9 mm long.\n\n## The rule\n\n- Two neighbour arcs whose ends are no more than `JOIN_MAX` (2.5 um, ten times `JOINT_TOL`) apart meet at the mean of the two ends. No connector move is written.\n- The rule applies only when the half gap is under a quarter of the chord of each arc. Then no end can pass the other, and no arc can read as a full circle.\n- Each moved end stands up to half the gap off its circle. The path margin now adds that half gap (`arc_gaps`, measured on the snapped first walk). When the margin is not zero, the path has a note for the joint shift.\n- The kerf and cover laws do not change. They read the recorded arcs, and they read an arc whose two end radii differ as the mean circle less half the difference. So they still check the exact drawing.\n- A wider gap, or an arc too short for the rule, keeps a connector line. That line is a real move of more than 2.5 um.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3959-wire-arc-joins.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Four-centre oval of tangent arcs (centres at (+-2 sqrt 2, 0) and (0, -+sqrt 3), no centre on the lattice), die, start hole at the origin. Before: 11 moves, of which 4 are connector lines of about 5e-9 mm. After: lead in, 5 arcs (the seam arc in two parts), lead out. The joint gaps are far under 1 nm, so the margin is zero and there is no margin note.\n- The same oval with the top arc lifted by 100 nm (a drawing joint gap at its two ends): the arcs join directly. The margin is 150.2 nm (100 nm drawing gap, 50 nm joint shift, 0.2 nm centre snap), and the note says \"up to 50.0 nm\".\n- The posted ISO program of the oval DXF: 5 `G3` blocks one after the other, no `G1` between them. Each motion block moves the wire by more than 1e-6 mm. Without the fix, this test fails with a `G1` block between two arcs.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib: `wire_edm::arc_tests::tangent_arcs_join_arc_to_arc_with_no_connector_move` (die and punch: no line between arcs, each move longer than the lattice, the moves chain, the kerf law passes; and an arc moved 2 um into the product still fails the kerf law).\n- `camcraft-motion` lib: `wire_edm::arc_tests::tangent_arcs_across_a_joint_gap_meet_at_its_mean_and_the_margin_holds_it`.\n- `camcraft-app` `wire_dxf_selection`: `arcs::tangent_arcs_post_arc_to_arc_with_no_block_that_stands_still` (posted ISO program).\n- The existing arc tests and law tests stay green, also `the_laws_catch_a_mutated_arc_path`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The goldens of #3937 (`crates/app/tests/golden/nc/{wire-iso,sodick-wire,g-edm}/wire_dxf_*`) have no arc-to-arc joint: the circle halves share their ends exactly, and in the punch each arc is between two lines. They stay byte-identical.\n\nEffect on another PR: #3958 (DXF splines and ellipses) adds `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_dxf_spline_die.nc` with 72 zero-length `G1` blocks. When #3958 and this PR are both on `main`, that golden loses those blocks. The PR that merges second regenerates it.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Sodick and G-EDM posts with a tangent arc chain (the posted test uses the generic ISO post; the change is in the toolpath, before the post).\n- A joint gap between `JOIN_MAX` and the walk's own limit. The walk does not make one today.\n\n## Gate\n\nAll on head `c7894675f` (Mac, debug unless stated):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 23 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (2.7 min). It includes `motion suites: lib`, `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `golden_cl`, `wire_post`, `wire_contour` and `wire_dxf_selection (arcs::)`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light` (release): 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- The pinning tests were red before the fix: the motion test found 4 connector lines of about 5e-9 mm; the posted test found a `G1` block between two `G3` blocks.\n\nHeavy step: none. This PR is `P7`, so it gets no targeted heavy step (\"Heavy lanes at review\").\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: two tangent arcs of a drawn profile now join arc to arc; the program has no `G1` block with no motion between them.\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #3937\nFixes #3959\n",
